    "result_text": "There's only the one test class, and the full build is green.\n\nDone. The change assigns the derived `membershipNumber` for owners.\n\nWhat I did:\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field), documented as `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression computing it from the owner's own fields: `customerCode + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`.\n\nSince `customerCode` (e.g. `SMI-0007`) and `registrationDate` (defaulted server-side on create) are always populated by the time the owner is serialized, this yields values like `SMI-0007-M26`. `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
